---
const { id = 'aws-architecture' } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="section aws-section" id={id} aria-labelledby={`${id}-title`}>
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="aws-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">AWS solutions architecture</p>
        <h2 id={`${id}-title`}>I see the whole system, not just the service diagram.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>I connect identity, APIs, compute, storage, delivery, and operations to the workload they serve. The important choices are where to put the boundary, what to automate, how the system fails, and what it costs to keep running.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="aws-grid" aria-label="AWS architecture areas">
      <article class="aws-card">
        <span class="aws-card-number">01 / Delivery</span>
        <h3>Get content to the right place.</h3>
        <p>CloudFront, S3, Route 53, and ACM: origin access, caching, domains, and certificates belong in one delivery decision.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="aws-card">
        <span class="aws-card-number">02 / Access</span>
        <h3>Put trust at the boundary.</h3>
        <p>Cognito, API Gateway, Lambda, and IAM: decide who can call an API, what each component can reach, and where authorization is enforced.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="aws-card">
        <span class="aws-card-number">03 / Workflows</span>
        <h3>Choose the right execution model.</h3>
        <p>Lambda, EventBridge, S3, and SES: connect requests, events, storage, and notifications without building a server fleet for intermittent work.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="aws-card">
        <span class="aws-card-number">04 / Operations</span>
        <h3>Design for life after launch.</h3>
        <p>CDK and CloudWatch help make infrastructure repeatable and behavior visible. I weigh reliability, security, and cost with the team before committing to a pattern.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="aws-close">My solutions architect lens: make the tradeoff explicit, choose the simplest architecture that meets the need, and stay accountable for how it runs.</p>
  </div>
</section>
